e week that stance took hold toward that flock, never a break; "the crown's protection withdrawn one step" is that price's resentment falling through grip into the deference band the liege's relief fork reads (§4.3), never a protection row — an outcome needs its occasion and an answer moves no `P` (§4.9's one path). All three are the REQUESTED family's (§8), under BD's `bodySpillEnabled` ∧ `polityEnabled` with BD's liege face `polityObligationsEnabled` (BD §13); the hold's `P` reads none of them. [CURED 2026-10-19 (fp-final r5) — `cure/D-BD-r4.md` §5's route to PL (the r4 verifier's ROUTED-UNAPPLIED FAIL: "PL has 0 hits for flock, sponsor or curb, so the row BD cites ('the fealty row PL already names for it') does not exist") · RULINGS-ROUND5 A.8 ("a REQUESTED `service_answered` under `body:` for a flock of the crown's creed; a rival creed's spread as defiance on PL17's line; the cost of curbing the liege's creed") — the door already returns rows of any closed kind (`cure/D-PL-r4.md` open item 1), so no kind and no prefix is added. REFINED, vetoable: (i) each edge judged by its own liege's creed (§3.1's idiom), routed to BD for its "the capital's patron"; (ii) the rival creed's defiance priced only on the court's own act of endowment — round 4's rule for harbouring (an act, never a stance by default, §4.8 (3)); (iii) the mirror priced on the active stances, and its "protection step" carried by deference, not a second input on the relief fork, which would count one defiance twice.]
